---
description: Electron main-process conventions for LDAP, IPC, and snapshots
globs: electron/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Electron main

- Use `ldapts` for binds and paged search. Implement `member` range retrieval (`member;range=0-1499` … until `*`).
- After bind, read rootDSE for `defaultNamingContext` unless the admin scoped an OU.
- Map socket/TLS/bind failures to admin language (VPN, port, credentials, certificate). Redact any password substring before sending errors to the renderer.
- Snapshots contain nodes, edges, findings — never bind passwords or `safeStorage` payloads.
- Keep graph build and finding detectors pure (no `BrowserWindow`, no `safeStorage`) so `npm run verify:fixture` can run them.
